# Docker build context is ./solution (see docker-compose.yml), not the repository
# root. Docker reads .dockerignore from the context root, which is why this file
# lives here rather than one level up.
#
# Everything outside solution/ -- docs/, plans/, ops/, .git/, .github/ -- is
# already outside the context and needs no exclusion. What remains is the build
# output and the test projects.

## Build output -- must never enter the image; stale bin/obj from the host
## can also poison the container build with wrong-RID artifacts.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/

## Editor / IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

## Tests
# Excluded deliberately: test projects are never compiled into a runtime image,
# and leaving them in the context means editing any test file invalidates the
# COPY layer and forces a needless image rebuild.
#
# Because FirmaData.sln lists the test projects but they are not in the context,
# a solution-level restore fails here:
#     dotnet restore FirmaData.sln
#     error MSB3202: The project file "...\FirmaData.Domain.Tests.csproj" was not found.
#
# The Dockerfiles therefore restore FirmaData.Build.slnf (solution filter, ships
# only src/ projects) instead. CI still uses the full FirmaData.sln so tests run.
tests/

## Test and coverage artifacts
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Cc]overage/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
*.trx
*.coverage

## Container definitions -- the Dockerfiles are passed to the daemon explicitly
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore

## Scratch, temp, secrets
scratch/
.scratch/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
.env
.env.*
*.local.json
appsettings.*.local.json

## OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Deliberately NOT ignored, despite being at the context root:
#   Directory.Build.props, Directory.Packages.props  -- central package management
#   .editorconfig                                    -- analyzer rules; excluding it
#     would let the container build pass where CI fails (warnings-as-errors)
#   FirmaData.Build.slnf                             -- REQUIRED; what the
#     Dockerfiles restore (see the Tests section above)
#   FirmaData.sln                                    -- the filter references it by
#     path, so it must be present even though it is not restored directly
